  "id": "Compound::DB00334 - Gene::1128",
  "verbalization": "Olanzapine is shown to interact with Hrh4, a protein that participates in multiple receptor activities, including G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor activity and acetylcholine receptor activity. These receptor activities are ultimately linked to Chrm1, a receptor involved in the regulation of cholinergic signaling. The evidence suggests that Olanzapine exerts its effects through a mechanism involving Hrh4, which modulates the activity of cholinergic receptors, potentially influencing the function of Chrm1. The consistent interaction across three paths, with similar scores, indicates a robust and reliable relationship between Olanzapine and Chrm1. The mechanism appears to involve Hrh4 as a key mediator, linking Olanzapine to the cholinergic system and its downstream effects on Chrm1. The integration of these pathways supports a mechanistic link that is both biologically plausible and consistent across different evidence sources.",
